"A siblinghold is a knight household founded by siblings, like the art'h by triplets."
"The art'h siblinghold was founded by Jeneth, Alis and Tesen, and lives on Rapport I."
"Spouses are its backbone: they bear and raise children and serve as wizards for knights and Rapport."
"The family is a dream and a duty that its members commit to by contract."
"Siblingholds are an uncommon arrangement in modern times."
"Children come in sets spanning three or four years, so several may choose the knight path together."
"Sets are timed so the knight parents can be home for life markers; the last art'h set was eighteen."
"Twins and triplets who become knights together do well; close companions help knights thrive."
"Written marriage contracts are kept in the house's manuscript library."
"The art'h land sits at the center of a massive corruption event of long ago."
"Its surviving dark-barked trees are a key part of the magic keeping Rapport I safe."
"The Primary's ancestors buried their dead under those trees, believing souls reach the Mother's heart."
"The land's magic welcomes those the family welcomes; members speak to the land about newcomers."
"An art'h leaving on a journey is ritually bound to the land at the old house, carrying it along."
"The land may give a rare living leaf to one it wishes to connect with, returned before a binding."
